<BaseLayout title="UNESCO World Heritage Sites in Algeria | Algeria Compass" description="Algeria’s seven UNESCO World Heritage Sites, from Djémila and Timgad to the Tassili n’Ajjer and the M’Zab Valley." image="/assets/img/timgad-trajan-arch.jpg" region="sahara">
  <Hero title="UNESCO World Heritage Sites in Algeria" eyebrow="Knowledge hub" text="Algeria’s seven UNESCO World Heritage Sites, from Djémila and Timgad to the Tassili n’Ajjer and the M’Zab Valley." image="/assets/img/timgad-trajan-arch.jpg" alt="The triumphal arch at Timgad, a UNESCO Roman city in Batna state, Algeria" />
  <Breadcrumbs items={[{name:'Home',href:'/'},{name:'UNESCO World Heritage Sites in Algeria'}]} />
  <section class="section"><div class="wrap" style="max-width:820px">
    <QuickAnswer text="Algeria holds seven UNESCO World Heritage Sites — more than most travellers expect. They span Roman cities (Djémila, Timgad, Tipaza), the Sahara's prehistoric rock-art plateau of Tassili n'Ajjer, the fortified M'Zab Valley, the Casbah of Algiers and the fortress of Beni Hammad." />
    <div class="prose">
      <p>Algeria holds seven UNESCO World Heritage Sites — more than most travellers expect. They span Roman cities (Djémila, Timgad, Tipaza), the Sahara's prehistoric rock-art plateau of Tassili n'Ajjer, the fortified M'Zab Valley, the Casbah of Algiers and the fortress of Beni Hammad.</p>
